pect_description (1.0)\n\nThe vehicle linkage is strong with ANPR hits. The suspect description is identical. The MO is similar but with differences in violence and target. The spatiotemporal proximity is moderate (1.6 km, 11 days). The target profile differs (woman vs elderly woman).\n\nThe score is 0.6924 (medium band). The prior pairs were high band (0.819, 0.7887).\n\nAs a Skeptic, I need to be strict. The question: is this link credible? The vehicle and suspect description match strongly. The MO is similar but not identical. The target difference could indicate evolving targeting (as the rationale suggests). The 11 days and 1.6 km is not extremely tight but not huge either.\n\nThe prior vetted answers show the Planner's rationale: \"The pair shows strong MO and suspect description matches with vehicle linkage, but moderate spatiotemporal proximity and differing victim profiles suggest possible same offenders with evolving targeting.\"\n\nThe Skeptic in prior answers approved the stronger pairs. For this medium-strength pair, I need to decide.\n\nFactors in favor:\n- Identical suspect description (1.0)\n- Strong vehicle linkage with ANPR evidence (0.85)\n- High MO similarity (0.75) - core MO same (approach, disguise, escape, offender count, target item, time band)\n- Geographic proximity (1.6 km)\n\nFactors against:\n- Target profile differs significantly (0.3) - woman vs elderly woman\n- Violence differs (push vs push_and_fall)\n- 11 days gap\n- No plate on second crime (but ANPR hits link vehicle)\n\nThe ANPR hits (ANPR-R0581767, ANPR-R0590687) are specific evidence linking the vehicle. That's strong.\n\nI think this is credible enough to approve, but with a critique noting the target difference and time gap. The prior Skeptic approved pairs with 7 days/1.5km and 2 days/3.5km. This is 11 days/1.6km. The time gap is larger but still within a plausible series window.\n\nI'll approve but with a critique highlighting the target profile difference and suggesting mo